-- title:
--   Leading residue at index -n equals ̄ G(0,0), -n dominant
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain that is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e, q \ge 1$ be natural numbers. Work in the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\varpi^{e}) = \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W/(X_0X_1 - C(\varpi^{e}))$, with quotient map `mk`. Let $x \ne 0$ be an element of this model, and let $ab = (a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ of zero constant coefficient such that $x$ is the class of $\mathrm{inU}\,a + \mathrm{inV}\,b$, where $\mathrm{inU}\,a$ has coefficient $a_{d_0}$ at $d$ when $d_1 = 0$ and $0$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{inV}\,b$ has coefficient $b_{d_1}$ at $d$ when $d_0 = 0$ and $0$ otherwise. Let $\gamma$ be a unit of the model, represented by a two-variable power series $G$, and let $n$ be a natural number with $x - \gamma \cdot (V(\varpi^{e}))^{n}$ in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\varpi^{e})\,\varpi$ (the class of $C(\varpi)$) and by $U(\varpi^{e})$. Then two conclusions hold. First, the leading residue at $\varpi$ of the normal-form coefficient $\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,(-n)$ — that coefficient being the $n$-th coefficient of $b$ for $n \ge 1$ and the constant coefficient of $a$ for $n = 0$, and the leading residue being $0$ if the coefficient vanishes and otherwise the residue of its unit part after dividing out the maximal power of $\varpi$ — equals the residue in the residue field of $W$ of the constant coefficient of $G$. Second, $-n$ lies in $\mathrm{dominantIndices}$ for the order function $w \mapsto q \cdot \mathrm{addVal}_W(w)$ with both weight parameters equal to $q e$ and the pair $ab$, i.e. the term order $q\,\mathrm{addVal}_W(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,(-n)) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\,(qe)\,(qe)\,(\mathrm{nfExponent}\,(-n))$ attains the infimum $\mathrm{repGaussOrder}$ of the corresponding quantities over all exponents $d$ for the series $\mathrm{inU}\,a + \mathrm{inV}\,b$.
--
--   This identifies, for an element of the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^{e})$ that is congruent to a unit multiple of $V^{n}$ modulo $(\varpi, U)$, the leading residue of its normal-form Laurent coefficient at index $-n$ with the residue of the constant term of any representative of the unit, and records that this index is dominant for the Gauss-type order attached to the weights $(qe, qe)$. It is used in the comparison of residues of the two coordinate ends of the model and in the computation of the leading residue of a characteristic-polynomial coefficient.
